	(text "look into how youre supposed to configure a pmos circuit.\ncurrently if you ran with this, when the nmos is off, the pmos\nwould be 'floating' causing issues.\n\nyou need to add a pull up resistor of soem sort, like i did in my\ncircuit.\n\nalso i highly suggest adding pull down resistors to youre nmos gates to ensure\nthat when you make them low, they 'actually' become low.\nit just a way to ensure the line actually hits 0V.\n\nalso add gate resistors for the nmos to protect the ic."
		(exclude_from_sim no)
		(at 78.232 72.898 0)
		(effects
			(font
				(size 1.27 1.27)
				(color 255 0 23 1)
			)
		)
